JA4 framework
=============

This framework computes JA4 client fingerprints, JA4S server fingerprints, and
JA4QUIC client fingerprints from the TLS events exposed by Zeek's SSL/TLS
analyzer. QUIC Initial packets are decrypted by the QUIC analyzer and produce
the same TLS events.

The ja4.log stream contains one row per fingerprint kind:

	kind fingerprint prefix raw ordered_fingerprint label uid ...

The uid field joins the rows to conn.log. The prefix field is the readable
tA/B/C section of the fingerprint, while raw contains the unhashed wire-order
cipher, extension, and signature-algorithm lists.

Published JA4 sorts cipher suites and extension types before hashing. This
fingerprint is available in the fingerprint field by default. The
ordered_fingerprint field preserves extension wire order and is always
available; redefine JA4::use_wire_extension_order to use it as the primary
fingerprint.

Labels can be assigned by populating JA4::prefix_labels (longest matching
prefix wins), calling JA4::add_prefix_label, or redefining
JA4::fingerprint_label.

Fingerprint results for repeated handshake shapes are cached. The cache is
bounded by JA4::max_cache_entries and oversized keys beyond
JA4::max_cache_key_length are not retained; cache hits avoid sorting and
hashing the cipher and extension lists again. Use JA4::clear_cache to drop
cached values.
